# Every kind of crash: the kernel reports the fault, and the shell starts
# again (an unknown kind lists them all).
program: shell
# DOSBox-X lets a write through CS go through (docs/emulators.md).
emulators: bochs mame
keys: crash help\ncrash gp\ncrash ud\ncrash de\ncrash ss\ncrash io\ncrash cli\n
keys: crash hlt\ncrash int\ncrash kernel\ncrash call\ncrash write\ncrash fpu\n
keys: crash tf\ncrash nt\n
timeout: 60
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>crash help
crash what? The kinds: gp ud de ss io cli hlt int kernel call write fpu tf nt
A:\>crash gp
crash: jump past the end of my code
@bochs rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0007:{crash_kinds.gp}
@mame rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0007:2000
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash ud
crash: an instruction that does not exist
rx286: program fault #UD at 0007:{crash_kinds.ud}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash de
crash: divide by zero
rx286: program fault #DE at 0007:{crash_kinds.de_f}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash ss
crash: push past the end of my stack
rx286: program fault #SS(0000) at 0007:{crash_kinds.ss_f}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash io
crash: read the keyboard's port myself
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0007:{crash_kinds.io}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash cli
crash: turn interrupts off
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0007:{crash_kinds.cli}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash hlt
crash: halt the CPU
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0007:{crash_kinds.hlt}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash int
crash: INT 32h, beyond the IDT
rx286: program fault #GP(0192) at 0007:{crash_kinds.int}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash kernel
crash: load the kernel's data selector
rx286: program fault #GP(0010) at 0007:{crash_kinds.kernel_f}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash call
crash: call into the kernel's code
rx286: program fault #GP(0008) at 0007:{crash_kinds.call}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash write
crash: write over my own code
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0007:{crash_kinds.write}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash fpu
crash: divide by zero on the 287, unmasked
@bochs rx286: program fault #MF at 0007:{crash_kinds.fpu_f}
@bochs rx286 shell, started again
@mame crash: no 287 error arrived; is there a 287?
A:\>crash tf
crash: set the trap flag
rx286: program fault #DB at 0007:{crash_kinds.tf_after}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>crash nt
crash: set NT and IRET
rx286: program fault #TS(0000) at 0007:{crash_kinds.nt_f}
rx286 shell, started again
A:\>
